-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":7,"section_title":"Uniform contact cancellation on an exact injection level","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:7bc474eeea6edeefa7d6d56d2f919d8dce22a2153c023b5dca19695429271af2","file":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/06b-contact-cancellation.tex","line":30,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"082e875afdfe0ff6c69966603163290c35780193a063deed6e92e76ae5eabb75","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/06b-contact-cancellation.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:7bc474eeea6edeefa7d6d56d2f919d8dce22a2153c023b5dca19695429271af2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/06b-contact-cancellation.tex#L30"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{n:coherent-contact}\nThere is an absolute constant $C_*>0$ such that for every dyadic\n$n=2^d\\ge2$, every $1\\le k<n$, and every partition\n$\\lambda=(n-k,\\beta)\\vdash n$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{n:coherent-contact-sharp}\n \\|T_n(\\lambda)\\|_{\\op}^2\n \\le \\min\\left\\{1,\\left(\\frac{C_*dk}{n}\\right)^{k/2}\\right\\}.\n\\end{equation}\nFor $k=1$ this operator is zero.  In particular, with an absolute\nconstant $C$ independent of $n,k,\\lambda$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{rec:coherent-contact-bound}\n \\|T_n(\\lambda)\\|_{\\op}^2\n \\le C^k(1+d)^{Ck}(k/n)^{k/2}.\n\\end{equation}\nThe same statements hold with the coordinate order reversed."}
